Relative to the ADR's PQDESC_V1 roadmap item, CS-10 adds four things worth keeping:
- bundling the ERC-20, names and selector roots as well as the descriptor root;
- an on-device confirm showing data_version plus a bundle fingerprint;
- a leaf type-domain byte;
- an image-carried minimum floor.

Neither the ADR nor CS-10 covers the following:
- atomic co-versioning of leaf count, Bloom, P73K and provenance with the root;
- page allocation in the frozen geometry;
- a power-cut-safe commit;
- post-install visibility of the catalogue version (invariant #10).
